    "done_when": "A measurement script at docs/research/data/crew-contract-baseline/measure.py reads Claude Code coordinator transcripts under ~/.claude/projects, read-only. It selects at least five sessions that loaded skills/reckon-build/SKILL.md on 2026-09-26, with the selection rule and the session ids printed. For each session it reports the input tokens spent loading SKILL.md and each reckon-build reference before that session's first `reckon crew dispatch` tool call. A load is either a Skill invocation's injected content or a Read of those files, and its token count comes from the usage figures the transcript records around the load, never estimated from characters. The script also prints the current word counts of the skill and of all references together, measured by the same rule the done-when uses.\n\nThe recorded log carries:\n- the per-session figures and their median;\n- the word counts;\n- the revision;\n- a first line naming revision, tree and command.\n\nIts absolute path is in the manifest with an EXIT= line. The node's fragment records the baseline figure, the method, and the ids of the sessions measured, so the section 3 rewrite is measured against a fixed number. The script writes nothing outside the node's own paths, and the committed output stays under 200 KB in total.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
